{"id": "EUVD-2026-80742", "enisaUuid": "e45b0323-ee25-3a58-a7b6-dd4b74f66d0b", "description": "If an attacker-controlled authoritative server can produce a negative answer that is exactly 65536 bytes, then a flaw in `named` results in a negative cache entry of 0 bytes. When this entry is subsequently read, `named` aborts.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T13:46:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T18:45:36", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-19667", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.29", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.26"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-19667", "GHSA-m9xv-gf7q-4vjg"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3412d7a4-7a1f-3694-a457-5a777925d2b8", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.0 \u22649.18.50"}, {"id": "64da5622-7543-3dd7-9ea0-976e12bb4bda", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.27"}, {"id": "8cd4538a-3b64-3fe0-8899-f9fff8c162c9", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}, {"id": "94ac6b0e-2e34-36b5-9fdb-11a2423880f5", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.27-S1"}, {"id": "ec69b603-7f28-3e12-971d-90150ce55b52", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.25"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "eb55f3d9-524d-36ac-ae77-9b64b3ad42ed", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}